|game_text=Plays on table. Always Thinking With Your Stomach, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl are canceled. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Mobilization Points is suspended.
|errata_history=This is version PC-E1 (2 of 4), 27 August 2021. It is not the current version; the current version is [[Don't Do That Again (Tatooine) (V) (Errata 3)]] (PC-E3). The image is the PC card image of this version.
* '''Original''' ([[Don't Do That Again (Tatooine) (V)]]): PC card image of 8 July 2018<ref name="ht-L_dontdothatagaintatooine-0">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/022435b/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/dontdothatagaintatooine.gif dontdothatagaintatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/022435b 022435b] (8 July 2018, “Set 9 load”).</ref>, no errata mark; lower-left name “•Don’t Do That Again (V)”. The PC first released this shield with [[Virtual Set 0]] / [[Virtual Set D]] on 24 September 2014. The PC's Holotable image set starts on 8 July 2018, so this is the earliest surviving PC card image; whether the 2014 release slip had the same words is not shown by it. Text: “Plays on table. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. While opponent occupies no battleground systems, Mobilization Points is suspended. “Missing” on Always Thinking With Your Stomach is treated as “landspeed = 0 for remainder of turn.””
* '''PC-E1''' (this page): PC card image of 27 August 2021<ref name="ht-L_dontdothatagaintatooine-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/649630f/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/dontdothatagaintatooine.gif dontdothatagaintatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/649630f 649630f] (27 August 2021, “200: Added *E* where missing and updated some game text”).</ref>, marked “E”; lower-left name “•Don’t Do That Again (V)”. What changed from the previous version: PC errata (image marked “E”): Always Thinking With Your Stomach, Ice Storm and Sandwhirl are now canceled outright; the “Missing” sentence is removed; “While opponent occupies no battleground systems” becomes “Unless opponent occupies a battleground system”. The set icon at the lower right changes from the diamond-shaped D to the round Virtual Set D icon. The commit that added it is titled “200: Added *E* where missing and updated some game text”; the [[Don't Do That Again (Reflections III) (V)|Reflections III-base printing]] had shown this text since 12 July 2020. Text: “Plays on table. Always Thinking With Your Stomach, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl are canceled. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Mobilization Points is suspended.”
* '''PC-E2''' ([[Don't Do That Again (Tatooine) (V) (Errata 2)]]): PC card image of 31 July 2022<ref name="ht-L_dontdothatagaintatooine-2">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/ab74419/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/dontdothatagaintatooine.gif dontdothatagaintatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/ab74419 ab74419] (31 July 2022, “updated hires gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Light/hires/dontdothatagaintatooine.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/594c3a0 594c3a0] (31 July 2022, “Set 0 Hi Res”).</ref>, marked “E1”; lower-left name “Don’t Do That Again (Tatooine)”. What changed from the previous version: re-rendered by the PC in its high-resolution card style (new frame, colours and typesetting); same words (new line breaks). The lower-left name now reads “Don’t Do That Again (Tatooine)” and the errata mark is printed as “E1”. The printed errata mark (“E1”) does not match this version's place in the release order (change 2 of this card): recorded as a [[Players Committee transcription errors#Errata marks that do not match the version (Virtual Modern)|PC transcription error]]. Text: “Plays on table. Always Thinking With Your Stomach, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl are canceled. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Mobilization Points is suspended.”
* '''PC-E3''' ([[Don't Do That Again (Tatooine) (V) (Errata 3)]]): PC card image of 22 July 2024<ref name="ht-L_dontdothatagaintatooine-3">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/6c22b09/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/dontdothatagaintatooine.gif dontdothatagaintatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/6c22b09 6c22b09] (22 July 2024, “Fixing case and making gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Light/hires/dontdothatagaintatooine.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/a546b30 a546b30] (21 July 2024, “Set 23 Errata”).</ref>, marked “E2”; lower-left name “Don’t Do That Again (Tatooine)”. What changed from the previous version: PC errata released with [[Virtual Set 23]] and the July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit<ref name="dskit2024">Players Committee, [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/DShieldUpdateKit_2024_July.pdf July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit] (PDF, 3 pages, “SWCCG Players Committee, July 2024”; file built 2 August 2024), released with [[Virtual Set 23]] (22 July 2024).</ref> (image marked “E2”): “Always Thinking With Your Stomach, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl are canceled.” becomes “Cancels Always Thinking With Your Stomach, He Hasn't Come Back Yet, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl.” (He Hasn't Come Back Yet added; moved to the start of the text). The printed errata mark (“E2”) does not match this version's place in the release order (change 3 of this card): recorded as a [[Players Committee transcription errors#Errata marks that do not match the version (Virtual Modern)|PC transcription error]]. Text: “Plays on table. Cancels Always Thinking With Your Stomach, He Hasn't Come Back Yet, Ice Storm, and Sandwhirl. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Mobilization Points is suspended.”
Versions follow Bill's rulings of 12 November 2026: every visible change on a PC card image is a version, numbered in release order; a printed errata mark that does not match that order is recorded as a PC transcription error.

